# Cross-repo siblings cloned by setup-dev-env at workspace-lock-pinned
# revisions (see codetracer-specs/Testing/Cross-Repo-CI-Integration.md).
#
# This list was empty while `config.nims` already carried a
# `--path:$config/../<repo>/...` switch for every entry below, so CI compiled
# with none of them on disk: `just lint` produced ~950 "cannot open file"
# errors and still reported success (the recipes pipe into `tee` and just's
# default shell has no pipefail). The list is now exactly the set of sibling
# path switches `config.nims` declares -- keep the two in step.

# Core: `isonim/...` plus the transitive deps isonim re-exports.
isonim
nim-everywhere
nim-stew
nim-faststreams

# Renderer adapters (RS-M2/M4/M5/M6). Each adapter module imports
# `isonim_<backend>/renderer`; the Linux scaffolds compile without the native
# shim, which is why these are compile-time paths and not run-time deps.
isonim-gpui
isonim-freya
isonim-cocoa
# `isonim_android/renderer` lives under isonim-android/nim-lib/src, and the
# broader package under isonim-android/src; config.nims adds both, one clone.
isonim-android

# RS-M2 streaming integration tests instantiate the canonical task_app demo
# from isonim-examples and reach isonim-tui's TerminalRenderer transitively.
isonim-examples
isonim-tui
nim-termctl
nim-pty
